error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_SHIFT` in `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 3: shift count >= width of type
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2128-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-its-unit-s-refusal.hero:16:5
     |
  16 |     constant K_SHIFT: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` line 3 reads `#define K_SHIFT (1 << 40)`
  note: C leaves this value undefined: a program reading `K_SHIFT` would read whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines

